          "image_source": "images/page_13_equation_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.501,
            0.113,
            0.622,
            0.182
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{array} { r l } {  { \\frac { 2 0 6 } { 8 2 4 } \\times \\frac { 1 0 0 } { \\mathcal { H } } } } \\\\ & { = 2 0 6 0 0 . } \\end{array}",
          "image_source": "images/page_13_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.198,
            0.801,
            0.257
          ],
          "content": "Using the meaning of multiplication and division, can you explain why multiplying by 5 is the same as dividing by 2 and multiplying by 10?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.816,
            0.189,
            0.903,
            0.247
          ],
          "content": "",
